.TH "ELEMENT.MOUSEDOWN_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.mousedown_event \- Element: mousedown event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]mousedown\f[B]\f[R] event is fired at an
\f[CR]Element\f[R] when a pointing device button is pressed while the
pointer is inside the element.
.PP
This differs from the \f[CR]click\f[R] event in that \f[CR]click\f[R] is
fired after a full click action occurs; that is, the mouse button is
pressed and released while the pointer remains inside the same element.
\f[CR]mousedown\f[R] is fired the moment the button is initially
pressed.
.PP
This behavior is different from \f[CR]pointerdown\f[R] events.
When using a physical mouse, \f[CR]mousedown\f[R] events fire whenever
any button on a mouse is pressed down.
\f[CR]pointerdown\f[R] events fire only upon the first button press;
subsequent button presses don\(cqt fire \f[CR]pointerdown\f[R] events.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqmousedown\(dq, (event) => { })

onmousedown = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MouseEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]UIEvent\f[R] and \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
See \f[CR]mousemove\f[R] event for example code.
.SH SEE ALSO
